WEBVTT

00:00:01.560 --> 00:00:09.560
Alright, so we have it so that it looks like
the player is running through the scene.

00:00:09.710 --> 00:00:14.240
What in fact, everything is
actually just flying out the player.

00:00:14.241 --> 00:00:17.321
So now what we're going
to do is we're actually

00:00:17.333 --> 00:00:19.900
going to use a spawn
manager to be able

00:00:20.050 --> 00:00:23.960
to create more obstacles
that fly at the player.

00:00:23.961 --> 00:00:26.563
So to do that, we're going
to go into our hierarchy

00:00:26.613 --> 00:00:32.880
and we can just right-click
and create empty.

00:00:32.881 --> 00:00:39.640
Now we have an empty game object
and this will be our spawn manager.

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:48.720
And then in our scripts, we're going
to make a spawn manager script.

00:00:48.721 --> 00:00:54.920
And then just make sure to click
and drag that onto our spawn manager.

00:00:54.921 --> 00:00:58.720
So now that we know it's
been added as a component.

00:00:58.721 --> 00:01:01.600
So we'll open our spawn manager up.

00:01:02.049 --> 00:01:07.200
So in our script, we're going to
need a reference to our obstacle.

00:01:07.201 --> 00:01:12.240
So we need to make it public so that
we can drop that reference in there.

00:01:12.264 --> 00:01:17.920
And since it's a prefab, we
have to use a game object.

00:01:17.921 --> 00:01:24.720
And then we'll just call
this obstacle prefab for now.

00:01:24.721 --> 00:01:26.520
And then close that.

00:01:26.521 --> 00:01:28.973
Now we're going to
create another variable,

00:01:28.985 --> 00:01:31.680
very similar to a variable
that we made before.

00:01:31.681 --> 00:01:37.400
So this will be private, so we can just
set it whenever we want inside of our code.

00:01:37.401 --> 00:01:42.880
It'll be a vector three
because we're doing a position.

00:01:42.881 --> 00:01:49.040
And this will be the spawn
position for our obstacles.

00:01:49.041 --> 00:01:56.640
And we'll set this to be a new vector
three since we're getting another position.

00:01:56.689 --> 00:02:00.180
And we'll set it to, let's
call it 25 on the X so

00:02:00.255 --> 00:02:04.120
that it's all the way on
the right side of the screen.

00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:07.800
We don't need it in the
air, so zero on the Y.

00:02:10.290 --> 00:02:17.640
And then we don't need any kind of depth
towards us, so we'll call it zero on the Z.

00:02:17.641 --> 00:02:20.761
And then in our start
method, we're going to create

00:02:20.811 --> 00:02:29.920
that prefab once again
using our instantiate method.

00:02:29.970 --> 00:02:35.720
So this way we can create clones
or copies of our obstacle prefab.

00:02:35.721 --> 00:02:41.800
The object that we're going to create is
our obstacle prefab, which we listed above.

00:02:41.801 --> 00:02:47.640
We're going to have it spawn at
the position that we set in our variable.

00:02:47.641 --> 00:02:50.419
And we want it to be
facing the same direction

00:02:50.431 --> 00:02:53.040
that we set it when
we created this prefab.

00:02:53.041 --> 00:02:58.840
So get the obstacle prefab.

00:02:58.841 --> 00:03:06.600
We're going to get its transform component
and we'll get the rotation of our prefab.

00:03:06.601 --> 00:03:10.341
So you can see back in
unity in our spawn manager

00:03:10.353 --> 00:03:14.801
script, it's updated to have
that instantiate method.

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:16.360
It's got our variables.

00:03:16.361 --> 00:03:18.521
So now when we
press play, our obstacle

00:03:18.533 --> 00:03:22.041
should fly at us and we
should create another one.

00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:28.804
And when we see one obstacle
interesting, so at the bottom

00:03:28.805 --> 00:03:33.880
here it says that there was an
unassigned reference exception.

00:03:33.881 --> 00:03:38.120
So this red exclamation point
means that it was an error.

00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:46.360
And it says that our obstacle prefab wasn't
assigned obstacle prefab of spawn manager.

00:03:46.361 --> 00:03:51.320
So I think actually what happened
in our spawn manager, I see.

00:03:51.321 --> 00:03:58.360
So I didn't actually drag the
obstacle prefab into the variable.

00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:04.960
So let me do that really quick, cool.

00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:08.080
So now when I press
play, now up there you go.

00:04:08.081 --> 00:04:09.081
So we have two.

00:04:09.230 --> 00:04:12.640
And I wonder if two are just going to fly
at us randomly from the screen, perfect.

00:04:12.641 --> 00:04:15.207
So since we're spawning
one of our obstacles

00:04:15.219 --> 00:04:17.740
through code, we
don't actually really need

00:04:17.741 --> 00:04:21.959
this obstacle anymore, that's just
about everything it's going to do.

00:04:21.960 --> 00:04:23.640
And we're not editing a massive amount.

00:04:23.641 --> 00:04:25.120
So we'll just remove that.

00:04:25.121 --> 00:04:32.880
So in that way, when we press play,
it spawns one and it flies at us, cool.

00:04:32.881 --> 00:04:36.371
So now what you're
going to do is create your

00:04:36.383 --> 00:04:43.240
own empty game object in your
project hierarchy, call it spawn manager.

00:04:43.241 --> 00:04:47.600
And then in your scripts, you're
going to make a spawn manager script.

00:04:47.601 --> 00:04:54.520
You're going to add that as a component to
the spawn manager game object in our scene.

00:04:54.521 --> 00:04:58.246
And then in our spawn
manager script, you're

00:04:58.258 --> 00:05:04.960
going to make a variable to get
the reference of our obstacle prefab.

00:05:04.961 --> 00:05:05.961
So it'll be public.

00:05:06.110 --> 00:05:08.360
So that way we can
actually attach a prefab to it.

00:05:08.960 --> 00:05:12.560
It'll be a game object since it's a prefab.

00:05:12.561 --> 00:05:17.200
We're going to make a private position
that we're going to spawn things at.

00:05:17.201 --> 00:05:22.200
So we're going to use the
coordinates 25, 0 and 0.

00:05:22.640 --> 00:05:26.398
And then we're going
to instantiate a new

00:05:26.410 --> 00:05:30.640
obstacle prefab at our
spawn position and make

00:05:30.641 --> 00:05:36.440
sure that it spawns at the rotation
that we had the prefab set up before.

00:05:36.441 --> 00:05:41.640
And then last but not least, don't do what
I did and make sure to drag your obstacle

00:05:41.690 --> 00:05:48.280
prefab into the obstacle prefab section
here in your spawn manager script.

00:05:48.281 --> 00:05:54.080
Now it's your turn.